    "intro_html":  "Balsamic vinegar does something to beef that salt alone cannot. It cuts the richness, it caramelizes into the gravy over a long cook, and it turns a plain chuck roast into something sweet, tangy, and a little bit fancy for the price of a bottle of vinegar. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e38 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 665 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.92\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
